review_comments:
Yes, exactly. I made a mistake. If you see #35511 (which has already been reviewed, and is more recent than this PR) I do the following in device init routine, which is exactly solving what you are highlighting now:

```
        if (cfg->trig_enabled) {
                if (lis2mdl_init_interrupt(dev) < 0) {
                        LOG_ERR("Failed to initialize interrupts");
                        return -EIO;
                }
        }
```
So, I think I could call init_interrupt only if ```cfg->gpio_drdy.port``` or ```cfg->gpio_int.port``` are != NULL. Those will be both null if irq-gpios property is missing in DT.

To be honest I think that a flag would be more clear, but I understand also your point to be smaller in size.

My last code is like:
```
if (cfg->gpio_drdy.port != NULL || cfg->gpio_int.port != NULL) {
    status = lis2dh_init_interrupt(dev);
    if (status < 0) {
        LOG_ERR("Failed to initialize interrupts.");
        return status;
    }
}
```
